From 22fd56a5593d01da6b8afbe93bb3a84c2120dabc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 10:27:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jm-v7 040: VK_EXT_conditional_rendering on v6/v7

The v9 JM predicate job (panlib_v9_cond_render, which rewrites the job
header types of a draw or dispatch to their recorded type or NULL) does
not depend on Valhall: job headers are the same on Bifrost. Build the
kernel for every JM arch, move cmd_cond_render_begin/end and the
Begin/EndConditionalRendering entry points out of the v9-only part of
jm/panvk_vX_cmd_draw.c, and wrap the v6/v7 draw entry points (direct,
indexed, indirect, indexed indirect, byte count) and dispatches in it.
Meta keeps saving/clearing the state on every arch (ClearAttachments
stays predicated), and the issued-batch reset runs before any batch of
the command buffer on v6/v7 too.

Secondaries are replayed into the primary on JM (vk_cmd_queue), so
inheritedConditionalRendering is exposed as on v9.

Needed by PanProbe tess_cond_state (CreateDevice returned
VK_ERROR_EXTENSION_NOT_PRESENT on v7).
